WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:05.002
First: the fixture says
soft match isn't blocked,

3
00:00:05.002 --> 00:00:07.750
and an approved matching
window ends today.

4
00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:10.875
What does the check report
tomorrow, if nothing changes?

5
00:00:10.875 --> 00:00:12.850
The answer is b: Fail.

6
00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:17.350
The day after the window's last day,
the same state is a Finding again.

7
00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.462
You saw that in step two of the lab.

8
00:00:19.462 --> 00:00:24.249
Second: a response comes back without
the block soft match enabled property.

9
00:00:24.249 --> 00:00:25.663
What does the check report?

10
00:00:25.663 --> 00:00:30.301
The answer is b: a Finding, because
a missing value reads as off.

11
00:00:30.301 --> 00:00:33.675
You saw that in step seven,
when the pass fixture failed.

12
00:00:33.675 --> 00:00:38.599
The module page has two more questions,
on why the check is left out of a default

13
00:00:38.599 --> 00:00:43.660
run and where a new HTTP call belongs, each
linked to the section that answers it.
